    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "PROBLEM — why care",
      "role_note": "the problem, the stakes — BEFORE the CLI",
      "narration_text": "Your model scores a ninety-two AUC and ships to the clinic. The radiologist sees a confidence score of eighty-five percent and trusts it. But the actual rate of true positives at that confidence level is fifty-three percent. That gap — between what the model claims and what it delivers — is calibration error. A high AUC tells you the model ranks patients correctly. It says nothing about whether the probabilities are true. This video shows you how to audit that gap with a calibration curve, and why the Brier score is the number you should be watching.",
      "visual_intent": "title card: AUC vs calibration — 'high AUC, broken probabilities'; PROBLEM beat, no terminal yet",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "AUC vs calibration — high AUC, broken probabilities",
            "topic": "COMPUTATIONAL SKEPTICISM",
            "segment": "Calibration Curves, taken apart.",
            "greeting": "",
            "runningText": "framing the problem…",
            "output": [],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Fable 5",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 28.42,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T16:51:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "ASK",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — the command typed",
      "narration_text": "In the terminal: ask Claude to generate synthetic binary classification data, train a logistic regression and a random forest, compute calibration curves using sklearn, score each with the Brier metric, and label which classifier is overconfident.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "claude \"Write a Python script:\n(1) generate synthetic binary classification\n    (1000 samples, 15% positive, sklearn)\n(2) train LogisticRegression + RandomForestClassifier\n(3) compute calibration curves (n_bins=10)\n(4) compute Brier scores\n(5) label which is overconfident\"",
            "topic": "COMPUTATIONAL SKEPTICISM — CALIBRATION",
            "segment": "CALIBRATION CURVE AUDITOR",
            "greeting": "",
            "runningText": "generating calibration audit script…",
            "output": [],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Fable 5",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 14.31,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T16:51:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "CODE",
      "role_note": "terminal (Onda) — read the output before running",
      "narration_text": "Read the code before trusting it. The key line is one assignment: P-P-V per bin equals fraction of positives — that's what sklearn's calibration underscore curve returns. The Brier score is the mean squared error between predicted probability and true label. Two lines that contain the entire audit.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeCodeBeat",
          "props": {
            "title": "calibration_audit.py",
            "code": "# calibration_audit.py  —  Claude Code output\nfrom sklearn.calibration import calibration_curve\nfrom sklearn.metrics import brier_score_loss\n\n# calibration_curve returns:\n#   fraction_of_positives (empirical rate per bin)\n#   mean_predicted_value  (mean predicted prob per bin)\nppv_per_bin, mean_pred = calibration_curve(\n    y_true, y_prob, n_bins=10\n)\n\n# Brier score: lower is better (0 = perfect)\nbrier = brier_score_loss(y_true, y_prob)\n\n# Overconfident: predicted prob > empirical rate at high end",
            "sparkLine": "CALIBRATION CURVE AUDITOR"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 16.81,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T16:51:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "OUTPUT — run",
      "role_note": "Manim animation: B04_CalibrationCurve",
      "narration_text": "Run it. The green curve is logistic regression — it hugs the diagonal, the model's stated probabilities match reality. The crimson curve is the random forest — at high predicted probabilities, the curve drops below the diagonal. When the model says eighty-five percent, the actual rate is seventy-eight. That's overconfidence. Same ranking performance, broken probability estimates.",
      "visual_intent": "Manim B04_CalibrationCurve: calibration curves for LogReg (green, well-calibrated) and RandomForest (crimson, overconfident at high end) against perfect diagonal; Brier scores annotated; gap arrow highlighting the overconfidence zone",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B04_CalibrationCurve",
          "file": "vox_scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 17,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 20.27,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B04_CalibrationCurve",
        "at": "2026-07-19T16:51:20"
      }
    },
